.TH tix-config-fmt 1  "fmt " 
.SH NAME
tix\-config\-fmt \- Rewrite the global config (or a ticket document) in tix\*(Aqs house style
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtix config fmt\fR [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-t\fR|\fB\-\-ticket\fR] [\fB\-\-check\fR] [\fB\-o\fR|\fB\-\-output\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-log\-level\fR] [\fB\-f\fR|\fB\-\-force\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Rewrite the global config (or a ticket document) in tix\*(Aqs house style
.PP
Every table becomes a headered `[section]` block. That includes inline tables written on purpose (`alpha = { remote = "…" }`) and dotted keys (`alpha.remote = "…"`), not only the one\-line shape older versions of tix collapsed sections into. Plugin tables are reformatted the same way and their data is left as it is. Inline tables inside arrays have no headered form and are left alone, as is anything already in house style. The document\*(Aqs data never changes, and no version is stamped.
.PP
Unlike ordinary writes, this rewrites the document wholesale, so comments and formatting are not guaranteed to survive. Comments near a reformatted table are moved above its new header where possible. The command asks before writing; `\-\-force` (or `\-\-yes`) skips the question.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<CONFIG>\fR
Path to the global config file (overrides TIX_CONFIG_PATH and the platform default)
.TP
\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-ticket\fR \fI<TICKET>\fR
Format a ticket\*(Aqs `.tix/ticket.toml` instead of the global config: a bare id resolved under the tickets directory, or a path (anything containing a separator, or `.`/`..`)
.TP
\fB\-\-check\fR
Write and print nothing; exit non\-zero when the document is not already formatted (for pre\-commit hooks and CI)
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-output\fR \fI<OUTPUT>\fR
Output format for commands that support it (also forwarded to plugins as \-\-tix\-output)
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
json
.IP \(bu 2
toml
.IP \(bu 2
default
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the formatted document to stdout instead of writing it
.TP
\fB\-\-log\-level\fR \fI<LOG_LEVEL>\fR
Set the log level (trace, debug, info, warn, error)
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-force\fR
Rewrite without confirming
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Set the log level to trace (shorthand for \-\-log\-level trace)
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Set the log level to warn (shorthand for \-\-log\-level warn)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
